da81665078","file":"preprints/Fontaine-Mazur-modularity-at-the-prime-2-October-6-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":20,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1a73f91bc7d5c20f63b6338387c5946fc96326cb7c62d05faca742f0e7ee8618","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Fontaine-Mazur-modularity-at-the-prime-2-October-6-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:b7d0cace2f5cf7af475df9b4a5a0c7e1df3348a5a8fdcb109487a7da81665078","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Fontaine-Mazur-modularity-at-the-prime-2-October-6-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L20"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet\n\\[\n r:G_{\\mathbb Q}\\longrightarrow\\GL_2(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_2)\n\\]\nbe continuous and irreducible. Suppose that \\(r\\) is odd, is\nunramified outside finitely many primes, and is de Rham at \\(2\\)\nwith distinct Hodge--Tate weights. Then \\(r\\) is isomorphic to\na Tate twist of the \\(2\\)-adic Galois representation associated\nwith a classical cuspidal eigenform."}
